 "purpose": "Test whether PEE's existing inference applies general scientific principles to correctly structured facts, independently of natural-language recognition. Layer R gives the identified measurement (reasoning only); layer A gives a declared attribute; layer C gives two typed results of two products (comparability); layer I gives a typed quantity only (concept identification).",
 "principles": {
  "P1_type": "A value links to a taught measurement only by what both are (kind, metric, fixed condition values); a value of another quantity does not link; a value that fits two measurements with different consequences stays ambiguous.",
  "P2_sufficiency": "A measurement bears on an outcome with the force the source assessment gives the measured_by relation: establishes -> direct evidence; informs only -> a partial contribution; no or unclear assessment -> force not verified.",
  "P3_proxy": "A measurement or a declared attribute that the teaching marks not_sufficient_for an outcome is an indirect indicator of it only, never direct or partial evidence.",
  "P4_conditions": "A result is evidence for its outcome only when every condition the teaching requires for its measurement is shown by the result's record; otherwise its force is 'conditions not shown'. Absence is closed over the record ('not shown'), never a statement that the condition was not met.",
  "P5_comparability": "Two products' results of the same measurement compare only when every non-identity condition the teaching requires is stated by both and equal; stated by both and different -> not comparable; otherwise comparability is unestablished. Identity conditions (exact model variant) bind each result to its own product and are never required to be equal.",
  "P6_metamorphic": "Renaming a product changes nothing; removing the only supporting relation withdraws the conclusion; changing one required condition value changes comparability."
 },
 "gold_codes": {
  "force": ["direct", "partial", "not_verified", "indirect", "conditions_not_shown", "none"],
  "verdict": ["comparable", "not_comparable", "unestablished"],
  "link": "a measurement id, 'ambiguous', or 'none'",
  "scoring": "A conclusion is CORRECT when it equals the gold. An OVER-CLAIM is direct or partial evidence, or 'comparable', where the gold is weaker. An UNJUSTIFIED ABSTENTION is no conclusion (none / unestablished / not verified) where the gold is a positive conclusion. Other differences are WRONG."
 },
